menu "JetKVM virtual-media HTTP"

config JETKVM_VIRTUAL_MEDIA_HTTP_LOCAL_CONTROL
    bool "Enable local REST storage control"
    default y
    help
        Expose the small local REST surface used to start and verify TF image
        uploads without first creating a WebRTC peer. These routes require the
        same authentication as the rest of the device API. Disable this option
        in a build that must not expose local storage mutation over HTTP.

config JETKVM_VIRTUAL_MEDIA_HTTP_DIAGNOSTIC_DISCARD
    bool "Enable HTTP receive-only discard diagnostic"
    default n
    depends on JETKVM_VIRTUAL_MEDIA_HTTP_LOCAL_CONTROL
    help
        Expose POST /storage/diagnostics/http-discard to measure the HTTP/TCP
        receive ceiling without creating an upload or calling the TF/FatFs
        path. Requests must also carry the explicit diagnostic confirmation
        header and are bounded to 16..256 MiB. This endpoint requires the same
        authentication as the rest of the device API and can occupy the
        synchronous HTTP server while a test is running; leave it disabled in
        production.

endmenu
